{
  "about": "What the workers' disk guards decide on Windows, tested against both: PathGuard (C#) through DiskGuardVectorTests and disk-guard.js through disk-guard.test.js. Each scenario is a made-up disk. 'links' maps a link to the text it holds, as the system reports it. 'aliases' maps a second name for an entry (a short name, or a name Windows trims) to the entry. A device's reserved name (CON, NUL, COM1 and the rest) is refused as the last name of a path, with any extension: older Windows opens the device there, wherever the path stands, and newer Windows only for the bare name, so neither guard leaves it to the system. 'refused' is true or false for both workers, or one answer for each: the C# worker follows no link inside a repository, and the TypeScript worker follows one that leads to a place it would read, as a package manager's links do.",
